PRIMARY RADIUS PRINCIPLE
The useful field resembles:

A REPAIR-READY MARGIN

not:

A GLOBAL PLASTICITY HORMONE.

Nearby tissue becomes:
temporarily easier to repurpose.

Distant mature tissue remains:
canalized.

RELATION TO H74
H74:

FAST SURPRISE SUPPRESSION
is local.

H75 adds:

SHORT-RANGE NEIGHBORHOOD SUPPRESSION.

In both cases:
slow canalization memory is preserved.

Thus:
damage can soften current expression
without:
erasing developmental history.

RELATION TO H33 / H54
H33:
wake recruitment must be locally bounded.

H54:
challenge recruitment must be locally bounded.

H75:
plasticity recruitment must also be locally bounded.

The same systems principle recurs:

LOCAL DISTURBANCE
SHOULD NOT
AUTOMATICALLY BECOME
GLOBAL ACTIVATION.

OUTSIDE-STATUS-QUO IMPLICATION
A developmental AI may benefit from:
SPATIAL PLASTICITY TOPOLOGY.

The region near damage can temporarily become:
more stem-like / repurposable

while:
remote computational tissue
stays specialized.

This is a software developmental mechanism,
not biological tissue implementation.

DECISION
AR-H75 is POSITIVE WITH A LONG-RANGE DE-DIFFERENTIATION LIMIT.

Supported synthetically:

- plasticity can be communicated locally;
- pre-softening a repair margin accelerates role reversal;
- slow canalization memory can remain intact while current commitment is suppressed;
- long-range plasticity causes severe collateral loss;
- a bounded two-hop field captures most of the adaptation-speed gain without global collapse;
- false injury still has a bounded local cost;
- larger field radius gives diminishing returns.

Not demonstrated:

- learned plasticity radius;
- source trust for injury emitters;
- moving / expanding damage;
- multiple simultaneous injury fields;
- interaction with cell division;
- functional regeneration rather than role reversal only.

